abstract: >-
  Lecture materials on machine learning interpretability for SCC5819 Topics
  in Artificial Intelligence, a graduate course at ICMC-USP taught by
  Prof. Andre Carlos Ponce de Leon Ferreira de Carvalho, following
  Christoph Molnar's Interpretable Machine Learning. Module 00 acquires,
  treats and documents the SRAG/SIVEP-Gripe surveillance base (Brazil,
  2019-2024), derives a COVID in-hospital mortality task with every decision
  recorded, and chooses the course model by a pre-registered selection
  study. Each method module is a fully reproducible walkthrough on that
  model, pairing a lecture notebook with a technical companion that
  measures the method's behaviour rather than restating its documentation.
  The modules share one model, one temporal split and one rule-picked
  patient, so they read as a single case: ceteris paribus profiles (01),
  individual conditional expectation curves (02), LIME (03, including a
  line-by-line validation of the lime package internals), counterfactual
  explanations (04) and SHAP (05).
